SUMMARY:The Bittersweet Lesson of Scaling in AI for Materials
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: AI has the potential to bring much-needed acceleratio
 n to the development of chemicals and materials for energy and sustainabil
 ity\, just like it has delivered intelligence gains in other fields. The p
 ath to success goes through scaling\, perhaps exclusively through scaling.
  Rich Sutton’s ‘bitter lesson’ states that “general methods that l
 everage computation are ultimately the most effective” in AI. The coroll
 aries are bittersweet in chemistry and materials.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
