 on
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Taylor Webb\, Department of Psychology\, Princeton Uni
 versityTalk Abstract: There is a longstanding tension in cognitive science
  between theories that emphasize the structured\, symbolic aspects of the 
 mind — drawing an analogy to traditional computer programs — and the e
 mergent properties of cognition that seem to be better explained by neural
  networks. The rise of AI systems that are powered by neural networks\, bu
 t that display many of the properties associated with symbolic cognitive m
 odels (e.g.\, compositionality\, reasoning) has reinvigorated this debate\
 , while leaving open
CATEGORIES:Natural and Artificial Minds
